# K23 (CLOSED 2026-08-17, [M4.6d]): the exact-minimum ambiguous-decomposition
# boundary. A 100-byte all-'a' subject against (a{10,20}){10,50} has exactly
# one valid decomposition (10 x 10) and the VM used to explore the whole
# ambiguous space, returning RX_ERR_STEPS. MINIMUM-REMAINING-LENGTH pruning
# (D51 ruling 1, docs/design/k23_impl/k23_design.md) cuts every position from
# which no accepting continuation can fit: measured <= 1 step, where the
# unpruned build (-fno-length-prune) still needs > 10^7.
#
# THIS FILE WAS THE KNOWN-FAIL RATCHET'S RESIDENT and moved here when the fix
# landed; the ratchet is what makes that move mandatory rather than optional.
# Oracle-verified (python re): span (0,100), group 1 (90,100). From the D27
# blinded quantifier corpus (its siblings: the other tests/base/d27_*.rxt).
# The MRL fix's own corpus, written from the goal by a second D27-blinded
# author, is tests/mrl/.
pattern (a{10,20}){10,50}
m "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa" 0 100
g 1 90 100
